# Design the task before styling the screen

- Identify the operator, current branch, primary action, frequency, and device from the request and nearby workflow. Read only relevant product constraints.
- Base decisions on usability, existing identity, and evidence appropriate to the task. Consult `DESIGN.md` when current project guidance calls for it and the file exists. Use design judgment within the existing identity.
- Reuse established patterns. For a new workflow or major redesign, use karman-ux-benchmark when a concrete design question needs evidence and karman-ui-design when it helps implement the chosen direction.
- A local field or visual fix normally needs the existing component and applicable framework docs. Reuse a previously established benchmark decision.
- Choose one direction, implement it, and briefly explain the meaningful tradeoff. Resolve ordinary font, spacing, hierarchy, and interaction choices autonomously within the task.

## Review the touched journey

Use [the collaboration agreement’s affected-flow checklist](../../Docs/COLLABORATION_WORKFLOW.md#6-ui-quality-in-the-affected-flow). For operational screens, make the current branch and record visible and keep the primary action easy to scan. For lists, distinguish no data from no matches and offer a useful filter reset with stable sorting.

## Finish with evidence appropriate to risk

Follow the [verification scope and ownership](../../Docs/COLLABORATION_WORKFLOW.md#4-proportionate-verification-and-cost). Use karman-ui-review for an applicable visual review and limit it to the relevant route, viewport, role, and boundary.
